// I'll use a simple method with switch on Zone string to return a config object\n    // or just separate methods to avoid introducing new public types if possible.\n    // A nested class `ZonePricing` is package-private, acceptable.\n    \n    private static final class ZonePricing {\n        final BigDecimal tier1; // <= 1\n        final BigDecimal tier2; // <= 5\n        final BigDecimal tier3; // <= 10\n        final BigDecimal over10Rate;\n        \n        ZonePricing(BigDecimal t1, BigDecimal t2, BigDecimal t3, BigDecimal rate) {\n            this.tier1 = t1;\n            this.tier2 = t2;\n            this.tier3 = t3;\n            this.over10Rate = rate;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Helper to get Pricing Config\n    private static ZonePricing getPricingConfig(String zone) {\n        if (ZONE_DOM.equals(zone)) {\n            return new ZonePricing(\n                new BigDecimal(\"12.00\"),\n                new BigDecimal(\"15.50\"),\n                new BigDecimal(\"19.90\"),\n                new BigDecimal(\"1.20\")\n            );\n        } else if (ZONE_EU.equals(zone)) {\n            return new ZonePricing(\n                new BigDecimal(\"29.00\"),\n                new BigDecimal(\"39.00\"),\n                new BigDecimal(\"55.00\"),\n                new BigDecimal(\"3.10\")\n            );\n        } else { // WORLD\n            return new ZonePricing(\n                new BigDecimal(\"59.00\"),\n                new BigDecimal(\"89.00\"),\n                new BigDecimal(\"129.00\"),\n                new BigDecimal(\"7.50\")\n            );\n        }\n    }\n\n    // ... implementation ...\n}\n```\n\n**Re-Checking Validation Logic:**\nOriginal:\n```java\n        for (int i = 0; i < parcels.size(); i++) {\n            Parcel p = parcels.get(i);\n            if (p.weightKg() <= 0 || Double.isNaN(p.weightKg()))\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" invalid weight\");\n            if (p.lengthCm() > 200 || p.widthCm() > 200 || p.heightCm() > 200)\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" too large\");\n            if (p.lengthCm() <= 0 || p.widthCm() <= 0 || p.heightCm() <= 0)\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" invalid size\");\n        }\n```\nMy helper `validateParcel`:\nMust receive index.\nMust perform checks in exact order.\n`weightKg` check uses `Double.isNaN`.\n\n**Re-Checking Free Shipping Logic:**\nOriginal:\n```java\n        BigDecimal ov = orderValue == null ? BigDecimal.ZERO : orderValue;\n        boolean freeBase = false;\n        if (zone.equals(\"DOM\") && ov.compareTo(new BigDecimal(\"200.00\")) > 0) freeBase = true;\n        if (promoCode != null && promoCode.equals(\"SHIPFREE\")) {\n            if (zone.equals(\"WORLD\")) {\n                if (warnings != null) warnings.add(\"promo SHIPFREE not valid for destination\");\n            } else if (!freeBase) {\n                freeBase = true;\n                if (warnings != null) warnings.add(\"promo SHIPFREE applied\");\n            }\n        }\n```\nMy helper `calculateFreeShippingStatus(String zone, BigDecimal orderValue, String promoCode, List<String> warnings)`:\n1.  Normalize `orderValue` to ZERO if null.\n2.  Init `freeBase` = false.\n3.  Check DOM + OV > 200.\n4.  Check Promo Code.\n5.  Manage side effects on `warnings`.\n6.  Return `freeBase`.\n\n**Re-Checking Cost Calculation:**\nOriginal:\n```java\n            double vol = (double) p.lengthCm() * p.widthCm() * p.heightCm() / 5000.0;\n            double w = Math.max(p.weightKg(), vol);\n            double bw = Math.ceil(w * 2) / 2.0;\n            BigDecimal base;\n            // Pricing logic...\n            \n            BigDecimal amount = BigDecimal.ZERO;\n            if (!freeBase) amount = amount.add(base);\n            \n            if (p.fragile()) {\n                if (zone.equals(\"WORLD\")) amount = amount.add(base.multiply(new BigDecimal(\"0.15\")));\n                else amount = amount.add(new BigDecimal(\"8.00\"));\n            }\n            if (p.lengthCm() > 120 || p.widthCm() > 120 || p.heightCm() > 120) {\n                amount = amount.add(new BigDecimal(\"25.00\"));\n                if (warnings != null) warnings.add(\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" oversize\");\n            }\n            amount = amount.setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP);\n```\nMy helper `calculateParcelAmount(Parcel p, String zone, double bw, boolean freeBase, int index, List<String> warnings)`:\nWait, the line string depends on `amount` after calculation.\nAlso `base` variable is used for fragile surcharge calculation even if `freeBase` is true (which zeroes out shipping cost in `amount`).\nSo I must calculate `base` regardless of `freeBase`.\n\n**One Detail:**\nOriginal: `String.format(Locale.ROOT, \"#%d %s %.1fkg %s\", i + 1, zone, bw, amount.toPlainString())`.\nNote `zone` is the string (\"DOM\", \"EU\", etc.).\nNote `bw` is double (e.g. 5.0).\nNote `amount` is formatted with `toPlainString()` (no scientific notation), but usually default for BigDecimal is plain unless it's huge/small exponent. Wait, `toPlainString()` is specifically used to avoid E notation.\n\n**Final checks:**\n- Package name: `shop.shipping`.\n- Class name: `ShippingCalculator`.\n- Records: `Parcel`, `Quote`.\n- Method: `quote`.\n- Single file output.\n- No public API changes.\n\nI will ensure all helper classes are `private static` nested classes or package-private to satisfy \"additional types must be nested or package-private\". I'll stick to private static nested to be cleaner within the class.\n\nOne edge case: `orderValue` null handling. Original does: `BigDecimal ov = orderValue == null ? BigDecimal.ZERO : orderValue;`. My helper must do the same.\nOriginal logic for warnings list: If `warnings` is null, checks `if (warnings != null)` before adding. My helpers must check this too.\n\nOne detail on `Math.ceil(w * 2) / 2.0`.\nIf `w = 1.2`, `w*2 = 2.4`, `ceil = 3.0`, `/2.0 = 1.5`.\nIf `w = 1.0`, `w*2 = 2.0`, `ceil = 2.0`, `/2.0 = 1.0`.\nI must ensure this calculation is preserved exactly in the helper.\n\nOne detail on `Math.ceil(bw - 10)` in pricing logic.\nSince `bw` comes from double math, `bw - 10` might be `0.5`. `ceil(0.5)` is `1.0`.\nOriginal: `BigDecimal.valueOf(Math.ceil(bw - 10))`.\nI should ensure I use the same double arithmetic there.\n\nOne detail on Exception Messages:\n\"no parcels\" (original: `if (parcels == null || parcels.isEmpty())`).\n\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" invalid weight\".\n\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" too large\".\n\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" invalid size\".\n\"promo SHIPFREE not valid for destination\".\n\"promo SHIPFREE applied\".\n\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" oversize\".\n\nI'm ready to write the code. I will structure it with clear static methods.\n\nOne small optimization/correction on `getPricingConfig`: Since this is used inside a loop, creating new `BigDecimal` objects inside the helper for config might be slightly inefficient but necessary for immutability if `ZonePricing` fields are final references to those constants. I'll just define static instances of the Constants or recreate them (BigDecimal overhead is negligible compared to IO usually, but reusing constants is better practice). I'll make the `ZonePricing` values reference pre-created constants.\n\nWait, I should check imports. `List`, `ArrayList`, `Collections`, `BigDecimal`, `RoundingMode`, `Locale`. All standard.\n\nLet's refine the `validateParcel` exception order again.\n1. `weightKg <= 0 || isNaN`\n2. `len > 200 || wid > 200 || hgt > 200`\n3. `len <= 0 || wid <= 0 || hgt <= 0`\n\nWait, what if `p.weightKg()` is NaN and `lengthCm()` is -10? The first check throws \"invalid weight\". Correct.\nWhat if `weight` is fine, `length` is 300 (>200) AND `-10` (<=0)?\nThe checks are:\n1. `> 200`. 300 > 200 -> True. Throws \"too large\".\nIt never reaches the `<= 0` check for that dimension. This is specific behavior to preserve.\nWhat if length is -5?\n`-5 > 200` (False).\nThen checks `<= 0`. `-5 <= 0` (True). Throws \"invalid size\".\nSo order of validation checks for dimensions matters strictly. `> 200` MUST come before `<= 0`.\n\nI will write a private method `validateParcel(Parcel p, int index)` that throws `IllegalArgumentException` directly.\nThe main loop iterates and calls this.\n\n```java\n        if (parcels == null || parcels.isEmpty()) {\n             throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"no parcels\");\n        }\n        for (int i = 0; i < parcels.size(); i++) {\n            validateParcel(parcels.get(i), i);\n        }\n```\nThis preserves the exact behavior.\n\nLet's organize the code.\n\n```java\npackage shop.shipping;\n\nimport java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.math.RoundingMode;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Locale;\n\npublic final class ShippingCalculator {\n\n    public record Parcel(double weightKg, int lengthCm, int widthCm, int heightCm, boolean fragile) {}\n\n    public record Quote(BigDecimal total, List<String> lines) {}\n\n    private static final String ZONE_DOM = \"DOM\";\n    private static final String ZONE_EU = \"EU\";\n    private static final String ZONE_WORLD = \"WORLD\";\n    \n    // Pricing Constants\n    private static final BigDecimal DOM_T1 = new BigDecimal(\"12.00\");\n    private static final BigDecimal DOM_T2 = new BigDecimal(\"15.50\");\n    private static final BigDecimal DOM_T3 = new BigDecimal(\"19.90\");\n    private static final BigDecimal DOM_RATE = new BigDecimal(\"1.20\");\n\n    private static final BigDecimal EU_T1 = new BigDecimal(\"29.00\");\n    private static final BigDecimal EU_T2 = new BigDecimal(\"39.00\");\n    private static final BigDecimal EU_T3 = new BigDecimal(\"55.00\");\n    private static final BigDecimal EU_RATE = new BigDecimal(\"3.10\");\n\n    private static final BigDecimal WORLD_T1 = new BigDecimal(\"59.00\");\n    private static final BigDecimal WORLD_T2 = new BigDecimal(\"89.00\");\n    private static final BigDecimal WORLD_T3 = new BigDecimal(\"129.00\");\n    private static final BigDecimal WORLD_RATE = new BigDecimal(\"7.50\");\n\n    // Thresholds\n    private static final int MAX_DIMENSION = 200;\n    private static final int OVERSIZE_THRESHOLD = 120;\n    private static final double VOLUMETRIC_DIVISOR = 5000.0;\n    private static final BigDecimal FREE_SHIPPING_ORDER_THRESHOLD = new BigDecimal(\"200.00\");\n\n    // Fragile Surcharges\n    private static final BigDecimal FRAGILE_FIXED_SURCHARGE = new BigDecimal(\"8.00\");\n    private static final BigDecimal FRAGILE_WORLD_FACTOR = new BigDecimal(\"0.15\");\n    \n    // Oversize Surcharge\n    private static final BigDecimal OVERSIZE_SURCHARGE = new BigDecimal(\"25.00\");\n\n    // Promo Code\n    private static final String PROMO_CODE = \"SHIPFREE\";\n\n    private ShippingCalculator() {}\n\n    public static Quote quote(String country, List<Parcel> parcels, BigDecimal orderValue,\n                              String promoCode, List<String> warnings) {\n        validateParcels(parcels);\n        \n        String zone = determineZone(country);\n        \n        BigDecimal normalizedOrderValue = orderValue == null ? BigDecimal.ZERO : orderValue;\n        boolean freeBase = false;\n        \n        if (ZONE_DOM.equals(zone) && normalizedOrderValue.compareTo(FREE_SHIPPING_ORDER_THRESHOLD) > 0) {\n            freeBase = true;\n        }\n        \n        if (PROMO_CODE.equals(promoCode)) {\n            if (ZONE_WORLD.equals(zone)) {\n                addWarning(warnings, WARN_PROMO_INVALID_DEST);\n            } else if (!freeBase) {\n                freeBase = true;\n                addWarning(warnings, WARN_PROMO_APPLIED);\n            }\n        }\n\n        List<String> lines = new ArrayList<>();\n        BigDecimal total = BigDecimal.ZERO;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < parcels.size(); i++) {\n            Parcel p = parcels.get(i);\n            double bw = calculateBillableWeight(p);\n            BigDecimal basePrice = calculateBasePrice(zone, bw);\n            \n            BigDecimal amount = BigDecimal.ZERO;\n            if (!freeBase) {\n                amount = amount.add(basePrice);\n            }\n            \n            // Fragile surcharge applied even if freeBase is true (basePrice logic used)\n            if (p.fragile()) {\n                if (ZONE_WORLD.equals(zone)) {\n                    amount = amount.add(basePrice.multiply(FRAGILE_WORLD_FACTOR));\n                } else {\n                    amount = amount.add(FRAGILE_FIXED_SURCHARGE);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // Oversize check\n            if (isOversized(p)) {\n                amount = amount.add(OVERSIZE_SURCHARGE);\n                addWarning(warnings, formatOversizeWarning(i + 1));\n            }\n\n            amount = amount.setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP);\n            \n            lines.add(formatLineString(i + 1, zone, bw, amount));\n            total = total.add(amount);\n        }\n\n        return new Quote(total, List.copyOf(lines));\n    }\n    \n    // ... helper methods ...\n}\n```\nWait, I need to check the original Promo Code logic again carefully.\nOriginal: `if (promoCode != null && promoCode.equals(\"SHIPFREE\"))`\nMy refactored snippet: `if (PROMO_CODE.equals(promoCode))`.\nIf `promoCode` is null, `equals` throws NPE? No, I wrote `PROMO_CODE.equals(promoCode)`. Since `PROMO_CODE` is not null, this handles null `promoCode` safely (returns false). But original was `promoCode != null && promoCode.equals...`.\nWait, String.equals(null) returns false. So `PROMO_CODE.equals(promoCode)` is safe and equivalent for checking nullity + content.\nWait, actually:\nOriginal: `if (promoCode != null && promoCode.equals(\"SHIPFREE\"))`.\nRefactored: `if (\"SHIPFREE\".equals(promoCode))` or `if (PROMO_CODE.equals(promoCode))`. Both are safe against null `promoCode`.\n\nHowever, there is a nuance in the original code block structure regarding side effects.\nOriginal:\n```java\n        if (promoCode != null && promoCode.equals(\"SHIPFREE\")) {\n            if (zone.equals(\"WORLD\")) {\n                if (warnings != null) warnings.add(\"promo SHIPFREE not valid for destination\");\n            } else if (!freeBase) {\n                freeBase = true;\n                if (warnings != null) warnings.add(\"promo SHIPFREE applied\");\n            }\n        }\n```\nMy structure:\n```java\n        if (PROMO_CODE.equals(promoCode)) {\n             // ...\n        }\n```\nThis is equivalent.\n\nOne small detail: `addWarning` helper should check `warnings != null`.\nAnd I need to define the warning messages.\n\nAnother detail: The order of warnings added.\n1. Promo invalid/warning (if applicable).\n2. Parcel loop. Inside parcel loop, Oversize warning added immediately after detection.\nThis matches my code structure (`calculateFreeBaseStatus` logic before loop, Oversize logic inside loop).\n\nWait, I need to check if `freeBase` is calculated *before* the promo code check in the original.\nOriginal:\n```java\n        boolean freeBase = false;\n        if (zone.equals(\"DOM\") && ov.compareTo(new BigDecimal(\"200.00\")) > 0) freeBase = true;\n        if (promoCode != null && promoCode.equals(\"SHIPFREE\")) {\n             // ... uses freeBase variable here!\n        }\n```\nYes, `freeBase` is potentially set by order value check BEFORE the promo code block evaluates. My refactored logic does this correctly (checks order value first).\n\nOne thing to double check:\nOriginal: `if (!freeBase) amount = amount.add(base);`\nMy code: `if (!freeBase) { amount = amount.add(basePrice); }`. Correct.\nThe `amount` starts at `BigDecimal.ZERO`.\nIf `freeBase` is true, `amount` remains 0 before surcharges.\nSurcharges are added to `amount`.\nOriginal: `amount = amount.add(base.multiply(...))` (WORLD Fragile) or `amount.add(\"8.00\")`.\nMy code matches this.\n\nDouble check imports. I used `List.copyOf`, which is Java 10+. Java 21 supports it. `record` is Java 14/16+. Supported.\n\nOne final verification on validation exception messages:\nOriginal: `\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" invalid weight\"`\nMy code should produce exactly this string.\n\nI will consolidate the constants into a private class or just static finals to make it readable. Static finals are fine for Java.\n\nOne detail: `List.copyOf` returns an unmodifiable list. Original used `new ArrayList<>(lines)`? No, original used `List.copyOf(lines)`. Wait, original:\n```java\n        return new Quote(total, List.copyOf(lines));\n```\nYes, it returns a copy. My code should do the same.\n\nFinal check on `validateParcel`:\nI must ensure I iterate in order and throw immediately.\nMy helper `validateParcels` iterates and calls `validateParcel`.\nIf `validateParcel` throws, loop stops. This matches original `for (int i = 0; ...)` throwing inside loop.\n\nOne tiny detail: `parcels == null || parcels.isEmpty()` check is at the very beginning of `quote`. My code does this first.\n\nOkay, ready to construct the final Java block.\n\n```java\npackage shop.shipping;\n\nimport java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.math.RoundingMode;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Locale;\n\npublic final class ShippingCalculator {\n    // Records...\n    \n    // ... Constants and Helpers ...\n}\n```\nWait, I should confirm the `warnings` parameter behavior again. \"Other services depend on all of it, including the behavior that looks odd.\"\nThis implies if they pass a list, they expect it to be mutated. If null, no mutation.\nMy helper `addWarning(List<String> warnings, String msg)` will check null.\n\nOne more thing: The original code uses `String` for zone (\"DOM\", \"EU\", \"WORLD\"). I should stick to Strings in the public-facing logic inside `quote` (e.g. in line generation) to ensure exact match. My internal constants are Strings matching these values.\n\nI will define a `PricingConfig` record internally to make the pricing switch cleaner, or just keep the variables and a switch statement returning the values. A switch on String with private records might be cleaner. Let's use a private static class `PricingTier`.\n\nActually, since I need to return specific BigDecimal objects (which are immutable), creating a config object that holds them is good practice to avoid passing 4 args to every pricing calc call.\n\nLet's do this.\n\n```java\n    private static class PricingConfig {\n        final BigDecimal tier1;\n        final BigDecimal tier2;\n        final BigDecimal tier3;\n        final BigDecimal rateOver10;\n        \n        PricingConfig(BigDecimal t1, BigDecimal t2, BigDecimal t3, BigDecimal rate) {\n            this.tier1 = t1;\n            this.tier2 = t2;\n            this.tier3 = t3;\n            this.rateOver10 = rate;\n        }\n    }\n```\n\nI'll put everything in the `ShippingCalculator` class.\n\nFinal check on package: `package shop.shipping;`.\n\nOne last thing: `BigDecimal.ZERO` is used in original. I should use it too for consistency, though literals work.\n`new BigDecimal(\"200.00\")` is used. I'll stick to string constructors for precision as in original.\n\nThe method signature `quote` includes `List<Parcel> parcels`. The input list might be modified? No, we read from it. The `warnings` list is written to.\nThe output `Quote` has `List<String> lines`. This is immutable (`List.copyOf`).\n\nI'm confident.\n\nOne edge case: `BigDecimal.valueOf(Math.ceil(bw - 10))` in original.\nMy helper should compute this exactly the same way.\n`bw` is a double. `bw - 10` is double. `Math.ceil` returns double. `valueOf` takes double.\nThis relies on floating point behavior. I will preserve this arithmetic.\n\nDouble check imports: `java.util.Locale` is needed for `toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT)` and `String.format`. `java.math.BigDecimal`, `RoundingMode`. `ArrayList`, `List`. All good.\n\nWait, the original code has:\n`if (parcels == null || parcels.isEmpty()) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"no parcels\");`\nThen loop `for (int i = 0; i < parcels.size(); i++)`.\nIf I extract validation into a method `validateParcels(List<Parcel> parcels)`, it should iterate and throw if needed.\nWait, if I separate validation logic, the order of checks inside the loop is preserved? Yes, because `validateParcel` throws immediately on failure for that parcel.\nWait, does the original code validate *all* parcels before processing any business logic?\nYes.\n1. Check null/empty.\n2. Loop 0..size: Validate p. If fail -> throw.\n3. Business Logic (Zone, Free Shipping).\n4. Loop 0..size: Calculate costs.\n\nSo if validation fails on index 1 (2nd parcel), the exception is thrown before Zone logic runs. My code must do this.\nIf I call `validateParcels` first, it loops and throws immediately on error. This matches.\n\nOne specific detail: \"parcels.size()\" in the loop condition vs iterator. The original uses index-based for loop to construct error message with `(i + 1)`. My validation helper should take index or iterate with index to provide `parcel #X`.\nThe `validateParcels` method I design will iterate and throw `IllegalArgumentException` with correct index.\nThis is safe.\n\n```java\n    private static void validateParcels(List<Parcel> parcels) {\n        if (parcels == null || parcels.isEmpty()) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"no parcels\");\n        }\n        for (int i = 0; i < parcels.size(); i++) {\n            validateParcel(parcels.get(i), i + 1); // passing 1-based index for message? \n            // Original: \"parcel #\" + (i + 1). So if I pass i+1, it's cleaner.\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static void validateParcel(Parcel p, int parcelNum) {\n        // weight check\n        if (p.weightKg() <= 0 || Double.isNaN(p.weightKg())) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"parcel #\" + parcelNum + \" invalid weight\");\n        }\n        // size max check\n        if (p.lengthCm() > MAX_DIMENSION || p.widthCm() > MAX_DIMENSION || p.heightCm() > MAX_DIMENSION) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"parcel #\" + parcelNum + \" too large\");\n        }\n        // size min check\n        if (p.lengthCm() <= 0 || p.widthCm() <= 0 || p.heightCm() <= 0) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"parcel #\" + parcelNum + \" invalid size\");\n        }\n    }\n```\nThis looks correct and preserves order.\n\nI will combine everything into the single block now.\n"},{"content":"```java\npackage shop.shipping;\n\nimport java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.math.RoundingMode;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Locale;\n\npublic final class ShippingCalculator {\n\n    public record Parcel(double weightKg, int lengthCm, int widthCm, int heightCm, boolean fragile) {}\n\n    public record Quote(BigDecimal total, List<String> lines) {}\n\n    // Constants for Configuration and Thresholds\n    private static final String[] EU_COUNTRIES = {\"DE\", \"CZ\", \"SK\", \"LT\", \"FR\", \"NL\"};\n    private static final double VOLUME_DIVISOR = 5000.0;\n    private static final int MAX_DIMENSION_CM = 200;\n    private static final int OVERSIZE_THRESHOLD_CM = 120;\n    private static final BigDecimal FREE_SHIPPING_ORDER_VALUE = new BigDecimal(\"200.00\");\n    private static final String PROMO_CODE_FREE = \"SHIPFREE\";\n    private static final BigDecimal OVERSIZE_FEE = new BigDecimal(\"25.00\");\n\n    // Helper Classes to encapsulate Zone-specific pricing rules\n    private static final class PricingTiers {\n        final BigDecimal priceTier1; // <= 1kg\n        final BigDecimal priceTier2; // <= 5kg\n        final BigDecimal priceTier3; // <= 10kg\n        final BigDecimal priceIncrementOver10; // > 10kg\n\n        private PricingTiers(BigDecimal t1, BigDecimal t2, BigDecimal t3, BigDecimal inc) {\n            this.priceTier1 = t1;\n            this.priceTier2 = t2;\n            this.priceTier3 = t3;\n            this.priceIncrementOver10 = inc;\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static final class FragileRules {\n        final boolean isPercentage;\n        final BigDecimal value;\n\n        private FragileRules(boolean percentage, BigDecimal value) {\n            this.isPercentage = percentage;\n            this.value = value;\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static final class ZoneConfig {\n        final String code;\n        final PricingTiers pricing;\n        final FragileRules fragileRule;\n\n        private ZoneConfig(String code, PricingTiers pricing, FragileRules fragileRule) {\n            this.code = code;\n            this.pricing = pricing;\n            this.fragileRule = fragileRule;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Initialize Zone Configurations\n    private static final ZoneConfig ZONE_DOM_CONFIG = new ZoneConfig(\n            \"DOM\",\n            new PricingTiers(new BigDecimal(\"12.00\"), new BigDecimal(\"15.50\"), new BigDecimal(\"19.90\"), new BigDecimal(\"1.20\")),\n            new FragileRules(false, new BigDecimal(\"8.00\"))\n    );\n\n    private static final ZoneConfig ZONE_EU_CONFIG = new ZoneConfig(\n            \"EU\",\n            new PricingTiers(new BigDecimal(\"29.00\"), new BigDecimal(\"39.00\"), new BigDecimal(\"55.00\"), new BigDecimal(\"3.10\")),\n            new FragileRules(false, new BigDecimal(\"8.00\"))\n    );\n\n    private static final ZoneConfig ZONE_WORLD_CONFIG = new ZoneConfig(\n            \"WORLD\",\n            new PricingTiers(new BigDecimal(\"59.00\"), new BigDecimal(\"89.00\"), new BigDecimal(\"129.00\"), new BigDecimal(\"7.50\")),\n            new FragileRules(true, new BigDecimal(\"0.15\"))\n    );\n\n    private ShippingCalculator() {}\n\n    public static Quote quote(String country, List<Parcel> parcels, BigDecimal orderValue,\n                              String promoCode, List<String> warnings) {\n        // 1. Validate Parcels (Preserves original exception behavior and order)\n        validateParcels(parcels);\n\n        // 2. Normalize Country and Determine Zone\n        final String normalizedCountry = normalizeCountry(country);\n        final ZoneConfig zoneConfig = determineZone(normalizedCountry);\n\n        // 3. Calculate Free Shipping Status (Modifies warnings list if applicable)\n        final boolean isFreeShipping = calculateFreeShippingStatus(\n                zoneConfig.code, orderValue, promoCode, warnings);\n\n        // 4. Process Parcels to generate line items and totals\n        final List<String> lineItems = new ArrayList<>();\n        BigDecimal runningTotal = BigDecimal.ZERO;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < parcels.size(); i++) {\n            Parcel parcel = parcels.get(i);\n            \n            // Calculate Billable Weight\n            final double billableWeight = calculateBillableWeight(parcel);\n            \n            // Calculate Base Price based on Zone and Weight\n            final BigDecimal basePrice = calculateBasePrice(zoneConfig, billableWeight);\n\n            // Start Amount Calculation\n            BigDecimal amount = BigDecimal.ZERO;\n            if (!isFreeShipping) {\n                amount = amount.add(basePrice);\n            }\n\n            // Apply Fragile Surcharge\n            if (parcel.fragile()) {\n                final BigDecimal fragileCost = calculateFragileSurcharge(zoneConfig, basePrice);\n                amount = amount.add(fragileCost);\n            }\n\n            // Apply Oversize Surcharge & Warning\n            if (isOversize(parcel)) {\n                amount = amount.add(OVERSIZE_FEE);\n                if (warnings != null) {\n                    warnings.add(\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" oversize\");\n                }\n            }\n\n            // Rounding per original spec\n            amount = amount.setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP);\n\n            // Create Line Item String\n            final String line = formatLineItem(i + 1, zoneConfig.code, billableWeight, amount);\n            lineItems.add(line);\n            \n            runningTotal = runningTotal.add(amount);\n        }\n\n        return new Quote(runningTotal, List.copyOf(lineItems));\n    }\n\n    // --- Validation Logic ---\n\n    private static void validateParcels(List<Parcel> parcels) {\n        if (parcels == null || parcels.isEmpty()) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"no parcels\");\n        }\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < parcels.size(); i++) {\n            Parcel p = parcels.get(i);\n            \n            // Check Weight first\n            if (p.weightKg() <= 0 || Double.isNaN(p.weightKg())) {\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" invalid weight\");\n            }\n\n            // Check Max Size second\n            if (p.lengthCm() > MAX_DIMENSION_CM || \n                p.widthCm() > MAX_DIMENSION_CM || \n                p.heightCm() > MAX_DIMENSION_CM) {\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" too large\");\n            }\n\n            // Check Min Size third\n            if (p.lengthCm() <= 0 || p.widthCm() <= 0 || p.heightCm() <= 0) {\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"parcel #\" + (i + 1) + \" invalid size\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static String normalizeCountry(String country) {\n        if (country == null || country.isBlank()) {\n            return \"PL\";\n        }\n        return country.trim().toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT);\n    }\n\n    private static ZoneConfig determineZone(String countryCode) {\n        if (\"PL\".equals(countryCode)) {\n            return ZONE_DOM_CONFIG;\n        }\n        \n        // Check EU countries\n        for (String euCountry : EU_COUNTRIES) {\n            if (euCountry.equals(countryCode)) {\n                return ZONE_EU_CONFIG;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        return ZONE_WORLD_CONFIG;\n    }\n\n    // --- Pricing & Calculation Logic ---\n\n    private static boolean calculateFreeShippingStatus(String zoneCode, BigDecimal orderValue, \n                                                       String promoCode, List<String> warnings) {\n        BigDecimal effectiveOrderValue = orderValue == null ? BigDecimal.ZERO : orderValue;\n        \n        boolean freeBase = false;\n        \n        // Check Value Threshold (DOM only)\n        if (\"DOM\".equals(zoneCode) && effectiveOrderValue.compareTo(FREE_SHIPPING_ORDER_VALUE) > 0) {\n            freeBase = true;\n        }\n\n        // Check Promo Code\n        if (PROMO_CODE_FREE.equals(promoCode)) {\n            if (\"WORLD\".equals(zoneCode)) {\n                if (warnings != null) {\n                    warnings.add(\"promo SHIPFREE not valid for destination\");\n                }\n            } else if (!freeBase) {\n                freeBase = true;\n                if (warnings != null) {\n                    warnings.add(\"promo SHIPFREE applied\");\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        return freeBase;\n    }\n\n    private static double calculateBillableWeight(Parcel p) {\n        double vol = (double) p.lengthCm() * p.widthCm() * p.heightCm() / VOLUME_DIVISOR;\n        double w = Math.max(p.weightKg(), vol);\n        // Rounds up to nearest 0.5kg logic: ceil(w * 2) / 2.0\n        return Math.ceil(w * 2) / 2.0;\n    }\n\n    private static BigDecimal calculateBasePrice(ZoneConfig config, double billableWeight) {\n        if (billableWeight <= 1.0) {\n            return config.pricing.priceTier1;\n        } else if (billableWeight <= 5.0) {\n            return config.pricing.priceTier2;\n        } else if (billableWeight <= 10.0) {\n            return config.pricing.priceTier3;\n        } else {\n            // Over 10kg: Base Tier 3 + Increment * ceil(weight - 10)\n            double extraKg = Math.ceil(billableWeight - 10.0);\n            BigDecimal baseExtra = config.pricing.priceIncrementOver10.multiply(BigDecimal.valueOf(extraKg));\n            return config.pricing.priceTier3.add(baseExtra);\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static BigDecimal calculateFragileSurcharge(ZoneConfig config, BigDecimal basePrice) {\n        if (config.fragileRule.isPercentage) {\n            // WORLD zone: 15% of Base Price\n            return basePrice.multiply(config.fragileRule.value);\n        } else {\n            // DOM/EU: Flat fee defined in rules\n            return config.fragileRule.value;\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static boolean isOversize(Parcel p) {\n        return p.lengthCm() > OVERSIZE_THRESHOLD_CM || \n               p.widthCm() > OVERSIZE_THRESHOLD_CM || \n               p.heightCm() > OVERSIZE_THRESHOLD_CM;\n    }\n\n    private static String formatLineItem(int index, String zoneCode, double bw, BigDecimal amount) {\n        return String.format(Locale.ROOT, \"#%d %s %.1fkg %s\", index, zoneCode, bw, amount.toPlainString());\n    }\n}\n```","reasoning":"The user wants me to refactor a legacy Java 21 class `ShippingCalculator`.\nHere are the specific requirements:\n1.  **Refactor for readability and maintainability**: Break long methods into smaller units, remove duplication, replace magic numbers/strings with constants/types.\n2.  **Hard Requirement: Behavior must stay EXACTLY the same**. This is crucial.\n    *   Same totals.\n    *   Same line strings.\n    *   Same warnings (order matters).\n    *   Same exceptions (types and messages).\n3.  **Keep public API unchanged**: Package name, class name, nested records (`Parcel`, `Quote`), method signature `quote`.\n4.  **Single File Output**: All additional types must be nested or package-private. Output the complete file in a single ```java``` block.\n5.  **Java 21**: I can use modern features (records are already used, maybe text blocks, etc., though records are fine).\n\nLet's analyze the existing code for issues to fix:\n*   **Magic Numbers/Strings**:\n    *   \"PL\", \"DE\", \"CZ\", \"SK\", \"LT\", \"FR\", \"NL\" for country codes.\n    *   \"DOM\", \"EU\", \"WORLD\" for zones.\n    *   Price t